<!--
  Main-site sitemap (static, served from /public).

  Two rules recorded here so this file stops drifting:
  1. Never list a URL that 301s. /gmb-checker redirected to /gmb-audit-tool,
     and Google reports redirecting sitemap entries as errors instead of
     recrawling the real page.
  2. lastmod must be the day the page actually changed, taken from the last
     commit touching that route's page.tsx, never a blanket "bump everything"
     date. A sitemap that cries wolf gets its dates ignored.

  /gmb-audit-tool carries lastmod 2026-09-15 on purpose: that is when its
  hardcoded AggregateRating ("4.9 from 127 reviews") was replaced with
  schema that only emits once real reviews are published. The fresh date is
  what nudges the recrawler to drop the stale star snippet from the SERP.

  Keep this comment ASCII only and free of double hyphens: XML forbids two
  consecutive dashes inside a comment, and a broken sitemap is worse than a
  stale one.
-->
